---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ContextWindowCalculator from '../../components/ContextWindowCalculator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Context Window Calculator"
  description="Check whether your text fits inside the context window of Claude, GPT-4o, Gemini, and Llama — before you hit an error."
>
  <ContextWindowCalculator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why context windows matter</h2>
  <p>
    Every AI model has a maximum number of tokens it can process in a single
    request — the context window. Send more than that, and the API call
    fails or the model silently truncates your input. This is especially
    easy to hit when you're feeding in long documents, chat history, or
    codebases.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this tool</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste your text length in characters, or estimate it.</li>
    <li>The tool converts that to an approximate token count.</li>
    <li>Compare against each model's context window to see what fits.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Why is the token estimate approximate?</strong> Tokenization
    depends on the specific tokenizer each model uses, and varies by
    language and content type (code tokenizes differently than prose). For
    an exact count, use a model-specific tokenizer library.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does context window include the output?</strong> For most
    models, yes — the context window is shared between your input and the
    model's response, so leave headroom for the output.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
